## Generated from capture responses/096.json -- the standard-edition
## freshly-created PMC profile as BSG's own server produced it. These are
## the starting Skills, hideout Areas and Bonuses a new profile must carry
## so the skills/hideout screens render and the stash gets its StashSize
## bonus. Values are standard-edition; other editions differ (a stated gap).
## Regenerate with tools .validate/genstarter.py if the corpus changes.

## NOT purely generated any more: hideout area **type 21**
## (`5df8a81f8f77747fcf5f5702`, 2 stages, `enabled: true`) is added by hand
## below.  Capture 096.json jumps 20 -> 22, so the generator omits it, but the
## database this server loads DOES serve it from `/client/hideout/areas` and
## SPT's own `templates/profiles.json` carries all 28 -- a profile missing the
## area has a hideout room the client is told exists and the player has no
## record for.  Shape copied verbatim from type 20 (level 0, inactive-but-
## present), which is what every other unbuilt area looks like.
## If genstarter.py is re-run, re-apply this.

## ALSO not generated: 17 skill ids from capture 096.json (a PRE-1.0 capture)
## were removed by hand.  MEASURED from the client's own
## `Logs/<ts>/... backend_000.log`, which logs `Can't find skill to upgrade:
## <id>` from `SkillManager..ctor` once per profile construction (22 times
## each in log_2026.08.27_12-*):
##   AdvancedModding Auctions Barter Cleanoperations FieldMedicine FirstAid
##   Freetrading Lockpicking Memory NightOps ProneMovement RecoilControl
##   Shadowconnections SilentOps Sniping Taskperformance WeaponModding
## NOTE all 17 ARE still members of `EFT.ESkillId` (67 members,
## `python tools/fldoff.py enum EFT.ESkillId`) -- the enum is NOT the oracle
## here and a check against it cannot fail.  The client's `SkillManager.Skills`
## array is a SUBSET of the enum; the log is the only measured source for it.
## Serving a dead id is log noise only, but it is 374 error lines per boot.
## The reverse direction (enum members we do NOT serve: AimMaster, DrawMaster,
## Misc, Bear*/Usec* faction skills) is UNRESOLVED -- BSG's own capture 096
## did not carry them either, and nothing measured says the client wants them.
## Do not add one without evidence.
## `tools/betacheck.py` case `skillids` re-reads the served profile and asserts
## none of the 17 came back; `--mutate skillids` proves it can fail.
